add('model-monodisperse-limit',6,'Radius-mean paragraph','model_limit','For a monodisperse sample, r1 = r3 = rh and μ1 = μ3 = 1. This is a theoretical limit, not the measured current dispersity.')
add('model-measured-moments',6,'Radius-mean paragraph','derived_study_result','The study reports average μ1 = 1.48 and μ3 = 0.82. These are study-level distribution-derived ratios, not a separately reported pair for each Table 1 sample.')
add('model-thresholds',6,'Radius-mean paragraph','model_criterion','The cited criteria μ1 >1.25 and μ3 <0.905 indicate coagulation-controlled growth. Preserve the strict inequalities; these are interpretive thresholds rather than measured recipe conditions.')
add('model-psi2',6,'Nondimensional cumulative-distribution paragraph','equation','ψ2(η) = Nv/N∞ = ∫η∞ ψ1(η) dv as printed; Nv = ∫v∞ n(v) dv is the number of particles larger than v. The first integral mixes dimensionless η with differential dv; retain the source notation and avoid a silent mathematical correction.')
